From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:20:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: query a cube storage image through its 2D array
 type

A cube or cube map array storage image is a 2D array view of its image,
and every load, store and atomic reads its descriptor through the 2D
array type. Its size query read the same descriptor through the cube
type the shader declared. Metal answers a query through the wrong
texture type only by chance: on an M1 Ultra the hardware reads the 2D
array's own fields, a cube map array's size included, which the
division by six then turns into cubes. Under MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1
every such query answers zero, and nothing reports it.

The bounds check in front of every image atomic is such a size query,
so under validation every atomic on a cube image was skipped and
returned zero, and imageSize() returned zero:
KHR-GLES31.core.shader_image_load_store.basic-allTargets-atomicFS,
atomicVS and atomicCS failed on their cube image, and
KHR-GLES31.core.texture_cube_map_array.texture_size_compute_sh read
[0][0][0]. The size query now reads the descriptor through the 2D
array type too, which answers the same values without validation and
the right ones under it.

kosmickrisp_validated_cube_storage runs atomics and size queries on a
cube and a cube map array storage image under MTL_SHADER_VALIDATION=1
and checks every result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
